From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Walsh <contact.me@thejustinwalsh.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:43:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] server: POST /v1/systemone, the System One decision API
 (openjev, lev, kev), from ggml-org #29818

Ported from ggml-org/llama.cpp PR 29818 (a4cb4c61fd, merged 2026-10-02, MIT) onto this tree, so ONE llama-server can serve
the Bonsai chat model and a decision model: a "decision model" is a plain model plus "<arch>.decision.*" GGUF metadata,
answered in one forward pass per question, no token generated.

Taken: server_decision_context (tools/server/server-decision.{h,cpp}: parse the questions and the state, render the
"systemone" chat template, tokenize, read the scores, calibrate with the model's temperatures, format the answer), the
task type SERVER_TASK_TYPE_DECISION with its result, the route and the shared prompt prefix between the questions of a
request (n_tokens_shared, the child slots continue from the parent's state), common_get_decision_type() and the
embedding mode for models that read the embeddings output (kev), qwen35's optional cls_out projection (lev/kev heads),
the converters (conversion/lev.py: Lev and Kev, which are LoRA adapters merged into the Qwen3.5 base; OpenJevModel in
conversion/qwen.py), the hparams-loader hook and jinja_str_or_json() in conversion/base.py, the Decision keys and
DecisionType in gguf-py, the server README section.

Adapted to this tree (older than the PR's base): the server still has llama_batch (no common_batch / llama_batch_ext), so
send_decision() reads the outputs from the llama_batch view; handle_media() keeps its accept_base64_uri argument and is
made non-static; this tree has no mtmd_helper_init_opt, fill_task() drops that argument; the cache reuse of a decision
task never goes past the first position whose embeddings are read.

Not taken: the laya and mmBERT models (the modern-bert decision head in src/models/modern-bert.cpp, the mmBERT pre-tokenizer
in llama-vocab, conversion/bert.py), the nimble model (PR 29844), the Python server tests (they download a Laya slice),
the HOWTO document.

Own checks: the server and test-reasoning-budget build; the real run of this API is in the next patch (clef), which uses
the same route. NOT RUN ON A GPU, and no openjev/lev/kev GGUF was available offline.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
